welcome to another episode of unlocking  lily so I believe that we are all  capable of extraordinary things when we  embrace who we truly are Evans currently  an investor in my business and he's  helping me grow my coaching and speaking  practice and I am so incredibly honored  to have you guys join me on my startup  journey firing someone is the right  thing for them and if you're holding on  to an employee that you know that is not  right for the job or for your company  you are actually doing them way more  harm than good because even if they  tried their hardest and you tried your  hardest at the most they're only gonna  operate at a mediocre level when they  could be extraordinary somewhere else  and let's fast-forward this 10 15 20 30  50 years even down the road and they are  looking back in their career and they  plagued with regret because they wish  they had worked for a different company  that they could really fulfill their  potential and you as a leader who knew  what the right thing was and still did  not take action because of the fear of  hurting their feelings you are  responsible for that pain and I know  what you're thinking this is extremely  harsh what about their family I don't  want to hurt this person's feelings  maybe I'll just let this drag on a  little bit longer and I know this  firsthand because I have gone through  this myself I was struggling to take  action on this decision for the longest  time you see I hired my first employee a  little less than a year ago and he's one  of the nicest people you would ever meet  he really cared about people and he went  above and beyond  to help people out but after having  several conversations with him I  realized that the job was simply not  right for him he was so much bigger than  the job he had all this passion and  talent and skills inside of him that he  was just simply not utilizing at the  position he was in but I was afraid to  take action because I feared that I'm  gonna hurt his feelings and I wanted to  be nice so I drag this along for three  months justifying why I should keep him  around and I made excuses no maybes  because I moved to Thailand that's why  things are not working out that well  maybe it's a timezone difference maybe  is that they were all just excuses  because I was afraid and eventually I  realized the more I drag this on the  worst things got until eventually I had  to make that call and fire him so if  you're standing in the crossroads right  now and you are afraid to make the  decision and to take action I want to  help you because I don't want you to  struggle the way I did so I want to  share with you the three steps in firing  your employee step number one get into  the right mindset I understand that this  is the nicest thing you can do now  you're actually doing them a huge favor  by letting them go because now they  could go fulfil their potential where  they were only operating at ten percent  of their potential at your company and I  know it's going to hurt and it's going  to suck when you have that conversation  with them and feelings could potentially  get hurt and you may have a negative  impact on their families but know that  that pain is only temporary because in  the long run this is the best thing for  them so that's a mindset that I needed  to get into because as much as I'm  pushing you to do this I needed the  extra push myself because I was  justifying remember what I talked about  earlier  I just kept on  imagining my employee being somewhere  else that he could really shine as the  amazing person that he is I just kept on  looking forward and not worried about  the fear that was attached to it and the  more I did that it brought me more  clarity and focus so that way I could  actually take action towards doing the  right thing step number two have the  tough conversation it's called a tough  conversation for a reason because it's  not easy for anybody this is where your  love your compassion any empathy needs  to come in the whole reason why you're  struggling to finally take action on  this decision is because you were  concerned about their feelings and you  did not want to hurt them and that's  what you need to lead with you need to  lead with that much honesty and love and  that's what I did when I finally had  that conversation I told him that I was  worried about his feelings that he cared  so much for his job that I didn't want  him to think that he was doing a poor  job it was just not right for him and  the reason why I struggled so much is  because I was concerned about his family  because I know how hard it is when your  entire family is relying on your stable  income and I did not want to cause any  negative impact on his life and sure it  was really uncomfortable it was  uncomfortable for me it was  uncomfortable for him and maybe feelings  were hurt  temporary but in the long run this is  the best thing for everybody and that's  a thing having a tough conversation is  easily avoidable but in this situation  you can't you cannot avoid this because  this is your path in helping them out  step number three be supportive think  about all the different things that you  can do to help them in their transition  in getting  job so for example for me I hired my  employee threw up work so I made sure I  gave him a five-star review on his  profile I also gave him an awesome  feedback to show the future employers  how amazing he was and how much he cared  about his work and lastly I referred my  reference so anytime a future employer  wanted to contact me for reference I  would make myself available and that's  the thing you were struggling with this  decision is because you cared so much  about them so your support needs to  extend way beyond their employment with  you so guys those are my three steps and  I know how difficult it is to be an  entrepreneur and firing an employee it's  probably one of the hardest things you  will ever do so I'm hoping by me sharing  my journey and the mistakes that I have  made is going to help you and lessen  that pain a little bit  and I'm a social shadow for crafty Beach  thank you so much for reading the  comments in my last episode your support  means a lot to me and finally the  question of the day is what is the one  decision that you're struggling with  right now leave in the comments below  and I'll join in on the discussion thank  you guys so much for watching and more  importantly being on this journey with  me as I grow as I learn as I go through  my ups and my downs it gives me the  comfort in knowing that you guys aren't  there for me every step of the way  so thank you so much again and I'll see  you guys very very soon if you had to  think of one word that's most important  to you or that sums you up or that would  be kind of like a little beacon if you  want to keep up with Lily's adventures  check out the last video we did it's  right next to me I think you're gonna  enjoy continue to believe and I'll see  you there so living the extraordinary  life means that you're out there saying  yes to a bunch of different things and  following your curiosity and really  jumping into the unknown  you
 

